 "info": {
  "description": "Bounded simulator subset of the official AWS Cost Explorer Service API (2017-10-25). Every other official operation returns HTTP 501 UnknownOperationException. Cost categories, anomaly monitors and anomaly subscriptions are stored configuration: no cost, usage, forecast, anomaly, recommendation, reservation, Savings Plans or tag-and-dimension value is read, computed or invented. Every Get cost, usage, forecast, anomaly and recommendation operation, the cost allocation tag, commitment analysis and cost comparison operations return UnknownOperationException with HTTP 501. Cost category rules are stored without being evaluated, so nothing is categorized: the effective start defaults to the first day of the current month, no ProcessingStatus, NumberOfRules or Values are reported, the EffectiveOn filter is accepted but only the current definition exists, and updating a definition replaces its rules and drops a default value or split charge rules the request omits. Updates and deletes keep no history, so deleting a category reports no EffectiveEnd. Anomaly monitors never evaluate: DimensionalValueCount stays 0 and LastEvaluatedDate is not reported. DIMENSIONAL monitors need a MonitorDimension, CUSTOM monitors a MonitorSpecification and no dimension. Anomaly subscriptions must name monitor ARNs in the right form, but the monitors are not looked up and a deleted monitor stays listed; subscribers are stored and never notified or confirmed, so no Status is reported. The MonitorArn filter of GetAnomalySubscriptions and the ThresholdExpression and Threshold rules of AWS are not evaluated. The service is global with ARNs that name no Region. A missing monitor or subscription is reported with ResourceNotFoundException instead of the official UnknownMonitorException and UnknownSubscriptionException, which the catalog cannot select. Tags are stored for all three kinds; resource counts are local limits, not Service Quotas.",
  "title": "AWS Cost Explorer (simulator catalog)",
  "version": "2017-10-25"
 },
